WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.520
- [Narrator] Located in Postojna, Slovenia

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.840
is a sturdy castle built
into a natural cavern,

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.534
halfway up a 400-foot cliff side.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:11.117
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.151 --> 00:00:18.030
Predjama Castle was built
in the thirteenth century,

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.510
in Gothic-styled architecture.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.360
However, after a siege
in the sixteenth century,

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.320
the exterior was reconstructed

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.873
and is what you see today.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.050
But there's more to this
castle than meets the eye.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.910
Beneath it lays the Postojna Cave Park.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.690
The caves are accessible
during May to September,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.900
and closed in the winter,

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.640
so as not to disturb the
hibernating local bats.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.560
The castle has changed ownership
throughout its history;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.320
however, the most famous
inhabiter was Erazem Lueger.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.500
He was a fifteenth century
Robin Hood-like character

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.410
who stole from the rich
to give to the needy.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.340
Today, the castle and caves are open

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.860
for the public to explore and learn more

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.973
about its previous colorful owners.

